WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.701
-Where should I put this thing?
-You can put it...

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:03.868
-Right in the front and center?
-Here, yeah.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.033
Front and center.
I mean...

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:07.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:10.100
-How's that look?

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.300
-You know, it's crazy.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.367
The last time
you were on the show,

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.300
you were on your way
to WrestleMania.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.167
And I said,
"Next time you come on my show,

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.267
you're going to have two belts."

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.434
-Whoo!

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.234
-Well...

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.534
You do have two belts.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.801
-Come on.

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:28.067
Come on, now.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.367
-He predicts the future,
as well.

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:32.534
-Yeah, I predict the future.
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:33.667
It just feels cool,
even just to hold that thing.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:34.834
-I know.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.801
-It just looks good there.
-It looks --

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:38.334
I'm leaving it here
for the whole rest of --

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:40.167
-Everybody, take a picture.
-Yeah, look at -- Yeah.

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:41.601
[ Audience cheers ]

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:46.067
-When you were a kid
dreaming about even wrestling,

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:48.367
did you ever think
you'd make it this big?

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:50.334
-[ Breathes deeply ]

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:52.267
I've always had great faith
and confidence

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:54.567
that I was someth--
I was going to be something.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:57.000
But you don't really know
what that thing is,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.767
and you don't really know
how far it's going to go.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.000
So, early on, I just wanted
to be a football player.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.200
You know?
-Yeah.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.701
-Watching the Super Bowl,
picturing myself --

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:05.968
you know,
"I'm going to Disney World!" --

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:07.033
you know and that moment.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.300
-Yeah, of course, yeah.
-You know?

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.801
-And then
I just tied into WrestleMania

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:12.634
and thinking that's exactly how
it's going to feel, you know?

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:14.367
-You get there,
but you don't expect to win

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:16.267
and actually be the champ.

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:18.267
-And be double champ, too.
-No, exactly.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:19.434
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:20.734
-And then you're making history.
-Thank you.

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.601
Yeah.

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:26.200
-Speaking of WrestleMania,
Royal Rumble is tomorrow, okay?

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.400
But that kicks off
the Road to WrestleMania.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.667
-That's right.

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:31.033
-And fans --
there's a lot of speculation

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:34.934
on the socials,
on the Twitters, on everything,

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:38.334
saying, maybe a possibility of
Roman Reigns versus The Rock?

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:39.634
-Ah. [ Chuckles ]

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:45.634
-That's been, like,
you know, the rumors,

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.033
and there's been
a huge buzz on that

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.601
for a long time now --
I mean, years -- for years now.

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:52.434
But it's really picked up
in the past couple years.

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.501
I believe he just came out
with a statement saying

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:57.767
that he's not going to be,
you know, ready in time,

00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:00.701
which -- that's the face that,
you know, everyone's making.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:03.100
Like, hold on, wait.
He trains every single day.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.367
-Yeah, that guy's ready for --
-We all -- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:05.601
-That guy's ready for anything.
-He's huge!

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:08.133
-Yeah, exactly. He's --
-But to his defense,

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.901
it's one thing
to train with weights

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:13.167
and you know, the body building
to look the part,

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:15.567
but to be able to get in the
ring and do a main-event match,

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:17.868
a championship match,
a universal, you know,

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:21.067
an undisputed
WWE Championship match,

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.434
it takes a lot of conditioning.

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:23.667
It beats up your body.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:25.334
So, there's more
that goes into it

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:26.968
than just training
in the weight room.

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:28.734
-It's a different way
to work out.

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.033
-It's a three hundred and --

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:32.367
It's a professional-athlete type
of situation,

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:34.534
where you have to condition,
you have to --

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:37.367
you know, he does two out
of the three things perfectly.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:40.300
His nutrition and his
weight training is on point.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.634
But you have to
condition yourself.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.000
And you got to be ready
to fall down.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.167
You know, that's --
You never get away from that.

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:47.634
-Especially if you're going up
against Roman Reigns.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.434
-Oh.
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah, yeah.

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:50.534
-That's number one, Dwayne.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:51.734
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:52.801
-When you're going up
against Roman Reigns,

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.133
you better get ready
to fall down.

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:55.968
-Yeah.
Who else is in the mix?

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:57.367
-Well,
that's the beauty of it now,

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.501
is we've got
so much stuff going on.

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.834
Right now, we got Sami Zayn
that's in the mix,

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:04.501
and within my Bloodline,
we've been doing

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:07.534
some beautiful TV
over the past six months.

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.968
We have another guy
by the name of Cody Rhodes

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:11.434
who's coming back from injury.

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:13.067
He was super white hot.

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:17.501
If you go back to -- I believe
it was a Hell in a Cell match

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:18.901
he had with Seth Rollins,

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:21.567
his pectoral muscle
was completely torn,

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.000
like in half.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.100
So, if you go back and look,
it's completely black and --

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.434
a giant bruise
covering this guy.

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:29.601
A fourth of his body
is completely broken,

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:30.868
and he goes out there,

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:32.801
and he puts on
like a 40-minute performance,

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:35.534
and just completely wins over
our entire fanbase.

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:37.801
So, a lot of guts,
a lot of courage out of him.

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.067
And he's going to be
coming back soon, too.

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.000
-You were telling me
something backstage.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.234
You were like --

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:44.667
-I'd smack all of them?
Yeah, that's --

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:46.367
-No, no,
you did say that, too, yeah.

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:48.033
But I was saying, like --
I was talking about, like,

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.367
what if I was a WWE Superstar,

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:52.033
what would my move be
or whatever, you know?

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:53.367
People probably do this.

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:54.567
But then you were like,

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.701
"You've got to have a fire-up.
You got to --"

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.400
What is a fire-up?

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.400
-Well, you got to have passion,
right? You know what I mean?

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.100
We can't just --
As a WWE Superstar,

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.501
you don't just slam a guy
and just sit there stoically --

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:05.567
you know what I mean?

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:07.467
Like, you've got to have
some emotion.

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:12.167
You got to be able to emit
energy, and that's what we do.

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.667
-Yeah.
-You got to be able to fire up.

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.300
You've got to able to lose
your, you know --

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.767
I don't want to start
cursing in here,

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:17.801
but you got to be able
to lose it, you know?

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:19.133
-You've got to lose your --

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:21.067
But do you say something
when you do it, or you just --

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:22.167
-Anything.

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:24.033
It's funny,
'cause, like, nowadays,

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:26.434
the default, like,
fire-up line is,

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:27.534
"Let's go!"

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:28.634
You hear it all the time.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.234
"Let's go! Let's effing --"

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:31.601
They always do the same thing,
right?

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.334
-Yeah. "Let's go."
-Yeah. "Let's go."

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:34.801
-But I could --
But maybe I could top --

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.167
I think I could top, "Let's go!"

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:37.801
-I think we can do better
than that.

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:39.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
I think we got enough

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:40.767
creative energy in here
to do better than that.

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:42.467
What do you got?

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:43.801
-What if --
'cause I was saying,

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:44.901
I was like -- my villain,

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:46.968
probably
my biggest thing I battle is --

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:50.033
with hosting a show is sleep --
people are falling asleep.

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:51.434
-Sleepy folks.
-Yeah.

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:54.934
-So what if my catchphrase
was, "Wake up"?

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:56.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.033
-Now we're talking.
-Right?

00:04:58.033 --> 00:04:59.834
-Human caffeine right here.
-Where do I --

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:01.067
Where do I -- Where do I look?

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.167
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:03.567
-I think down the pipe.

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:05.334
You got like six of them here,
so pick one.

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:07.534
[ Drumroll ]

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:10.334
♪♪

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:12.801
-Waaaake...

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:14.467
Wake up!

00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:15.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:16.767
Wake up!

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:18.133
-That's what I'm talking about.
Yeah!

00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:21.534
-Wake up! Wake up!

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:24.234
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:25.367
[ Music ends ]

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:26.834
Wake up!

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:29.100
-Hey.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.667
He kind of built it, too.
-I'm exhausted.

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.133
-He hit that, "Waaaake..."

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:33.367
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah, I built it.
-Yeah.

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:34.534
-Now I hurt something.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:35.934
I think the left side of my body
is bruised.

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:39.000
-Oh, no.
-It's bruised.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.834
Can we talk Royal Rumble?

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:42.033
-Please. Let's do it.

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:43.834
-You're facing off
against Kevin Owens.

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:46.100
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah.
-Wow.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:47.234
[ Chuckling ] Wow. Really?

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:48.634
[ Audience booing ]
-Yes.

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:50.200
-Yeah. What's -- Any --

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.300
What's your strategy
going into this?

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.934
-Don't change anything.

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:56.734
-[ Laughs ]
What do you mean?

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:59.133
-I've been beating up
Kevin Owens for years now.

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:00.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:00.968 --> 00:06:03.334
So...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.334 --> 00:06:06.200
Let me give this guy his due --

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.868
this is a tough, sturdy guy,
you know?

00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:09.200
And he's a little crazy.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.734
He's willing to do
anything out there.

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:11.934
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:13.868
But I've faced him a few times,

00:06:13.868 --> 00:06:15.901
and I've been pretty successful,

00:06:15.901 --> 00:06:18.167
So, for me, you know,
I just feel like,

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:19.367
as long
as I don't change anything,

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:20.701
if it's not broke,
don't break it --

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:22.634
just stay in the same system.

00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:23.968
Go out there and do what I do.

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:26.434
And pretty much, I feel like
I'm genetically coded

00:06:26.434 --> 00:06:29.534
to beat
Kevin Owens every time.

00:06:29.534 --> 00:06:31.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's like -- It's like --

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:33.300
It's like the small print
in my DNA.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:35.033
-Yeah.
-Yep, beat Kevin Owens?

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:36.467
Yeah, check. Done.
-You got this.

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:37.567
-Yeah.
-Alright.

00:06:37.567 --> 00:06:40.033
Kevin, if you're watching,
wake up.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:41.467
[ Laughter ]
-Wake up.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.934
-Roman Reigns, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:45.300
The Road to WrestleMania
kicks off tomorrow

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.334
at the Royal Rumble,

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:48.467
which you can see live
on Peacock.

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:50.968
We'll be right back
with stand-up from Cathy Ladman.

00:06:50.968 --> 00:06:52.300
Stick around.
[ Cheers and applause ]

